fig2: tailocin start from trpE to trpG…

our seq of tailocin currently used is 18057bp length, covered the genes from the 6th gene block in p25.c2 from the grey trpE, from 2698913 to 2716969.

trpE

1. p25.c2 has trpE (2694503-2695984, 1481bp), 
2. then a small one (2696041-2696130, 89bp), 
3. then a big (2696309-2698240, 1931bp), 

4-5: three small ones (2698353 2698595, 242bp); (2698642 2698824, 182bp); 

6: (2698913 2699170, 257bp). 

to 

gene 2716460 2716969 which is the one before trpG:

trpG 2717365 2717964

so now we are using tailocin:2698913-2716969


 this is from the supp of science paper, talia zenodo: https://zenodo.org/records/10729592 ./Tnseq/
the tailocin region is not annotated, but i found by minimap the currently used Tailocin seq its fully mapped with a deletion of G in the middle, to strand - 2698913 to 2716969 in the one contig fasta. now the length is 18056, end with TA like before, while the 2698913 in gff is a start of hypotheitcal protein, before which, there are several more genes, then its the trpE gene. The 2716969 is the end of a gene right before the trpG. And according to the fig2B in the science paper, the tailocin region is start with trpE, ends with trpG...
